course: dictionary
lesson: 13044
title: Saying farewell
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A farewell is a goodbye. You can say «Farewell!» to someone, or you can talk about a farewell as a thing that happens. «Farewell, my friend, and safe travels!» The speaker is saying goodbye to a friend who is going on a journey.
explain: Farewell can be a noun, a word for the act of saying goodbye. «We said our farewells at the station.» Here, farewells are the goodbyes that people said to each other before the train left.
explain: Farewell can also be an adjective, a describing word. «The class held a farewell party for Mr Lee.» The party was done to say goodbye, because Mr Lee was leaving the school.
explain: You will often see farewell in old stories and poems, where it sounds formal. Everyday people usually say «goodbye» or «bye». Think of farewell as a slightly fancier, more serious way to say goodbye.
fact: Farewell means goodbye.
fact: «Farewell» is an exclamation when you say it alone, as in «Farewell!»
fact: As a noun, farewell means the act of saying goodbye, and it is often used in the plural: farewells.
fact: «Bid farewell» means say goodbye, as in «She bid farewell to her family».
fact: A «farewell assembly» is a school gathering held to say goodbye when Year 6 leaves or a teacher retires.
exercise: «Farewell, my friend, and safe travels!» What does farewell mean here? | *Goodbye | Thank you very much | Come back soon | Hello, nice to meet you
exercise: «We said our farewells at the station.» What is a farewell in this sentence? | *The act of saying goodbye | A ticket for a train | Hot food eaten on a train | A loud cheer for the driver
exercise: «The class held a farewell party for Mr Lee.» What does farewell tell you about the party? | The party is very late | *The party is held to say goodbye | The party is held on a farm | The party is for a birthday
test: Which phrase means say goodbye? | *bid farewell | Clap your hands | Wave a flag | Share a snack
test: In which sentence is farewell a noun? | A farewell party was held for Year 6. | Farewell, and take care! | *They gave Mr Lee a warm farewell.
exam: In «Farewell!», what kind of word is farewell when it is said alone? | *A noun, a word for a thing or act | A verb, a word for doing something | A question, a word that asks something | An exclamation, a word said on its own to say goodbye
